{
  // The third subtree of @3d/shared allowed a library beyond `lib: ["ES2022"]`,
  // and the only one allowed Rapier.
  //
  // Everything dynamic and replicated lives here. A grenade, a rocket, a care
  // package and a corpse are one mechanism: a rigid body created from an
  // authoritative spawn, stepped once per server tick on both ends, and — where
  // gameplay reads it — corrected by the server. Two implementations of that
  // would diverge, and a diverged grenade is a player killed by an explosion
  // that happened somewhere else. It is here for the reason `sim/` is here.
  //
  // three.js is allowed for the reason rig/ has it: a ragdoll reads a
  // CharacterRig's bind pose off a scene graph and writes the result back onto
  // its bones. Rapier is allowed as a physics library, never as a loop — no
  // requestAnimationFrame, no wall clock, `world.timestep` is `1 / tickRate`,
  // and `step()` is called exactly once per server tick on both ends.
  //
  // Note what is NOT relaxed: no DOM lib and no ambient @types, exactly as
  // tsconfig.json. Only the two imports are new.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "types": []
  },
  "include": ["src/physics", "src/platform.d.ts"]
}
